+# 🏛 PEG-006 — Living Kernel Governance Integration
+
+```yaml
+document:
+  id: PEG-006
+  title: Living Kernel Governance Integration
+version: 1.0.0
+status: canonical
+layer: governance
+authority: PALACO Governance Architecture
+```
+
+## Authority boundary
+
+PEG-006 is the canonical governance architecture for the Living Kernel.
+It establishes the contract that governance must precede execution. It does
+not claim runtime enforcement until the corresponding kernel implementation
+and verification gates pass.
+
+## Control plane
+
+```text
+Living Kernel
+      ↓
+Governance Control Plane
+      ├── TRIAS
+      ├── Oracle
+      └── Mentor
+      ↓
+Certification Core
+      ↓
+Quay Provenance
+      ↓
+Execution Permit
+      ↓
+Execution Guard
+      ↓
+Kernel Action
+```
+
+## T-006-001 — Execution Permit hardening
+
+The execution boundary is no longer an `approved: bool` claim. A valid
+permit requires:
+
+```text
+valid certification
+∧ valid evidence
+∧ valid authority
+∧ valid time window
+∧ active permit state
+∧ valid target
+```
+
+The Rust type-level model is implemented in
+`crates/palaco-kernel/src/governance.rs`.
+
+## PEG-006.1 — StateProof
+
+Every governed state transition must be representable by a proof containing:
+
+* state identity;
+* parent state;
+* transition hash;
+* certification hash;
+* evidence hash;
+* timestamp;
+* integrity proof.
+
+Quay remains the historical provenance authority.
+
+## Security rule
+
+```text
+No valid permit
+    → DENY
+
+No valid evidence
+    → DENY
+
+No valid certification
+    → DENY
+
+Expired permit
+    → DENY
+```
+
+## Seven Wonders
+
+PEG-006 binds governance across:
+
+* Wonder I — LOGO;
